//! The `animation-trigger` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! specifies whether [CSS
//! animations](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Animations) declared on an
//! element are triggered animations (or not) and, if so, what their triggers are and how they should
//! behave when the trigger becomes active or inactive. This is used to create [scroll-triggered
//! animations](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Animation_triggers/Using_scroll-triggered_animations).
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: [ none | [ <dashed-ident> <animation-action>+ ]+ ]#
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/animation-triggers-1/#propdef-animation-trigger
